Severity: WARN
Category: packages
Check: check_repos
Fix: Drop the source or move to its successor.
References: sources.list(5), dnf(8), zypper(8), pacman.conf(5), apk(8)
Controls: CIS 7.3, 7.4; NIST SI-2; ISO 8.8; CE Security update management

A package source has not published, or this host has not fetched
it, for longer than Tigris_Repos_MaxAge days (180 by default): its
newest index is older than that and no suite of it changed since,
so the packages installed from it sit unpatched while the manager
says the system is up to date. The source may have moved or died,
or this host's refresh of it fails (a rotated signing key, a
proxy, a mirror it no longer reaches). Each repository
is judged by its newest suite: a release pocket never changes by
design, its updates do. dnf and zypper repositories are judged with
the others from the same host, so Fedora's fedora and openSUSE's
repo-oss, frozen at release, count as alive while their updates
repositories are; a host serving many publishers (OBS, COPR) is
split by project. Local repositories (file:, cd: and the like) and
openh264 codec repositories are not judged. Drop the source, move
to its successor, or track its -updates suite too.
